1
00:00:00,257 --> 00:00:02,270
Olivia needs complete handoffs.

2
00:00:02,616 --> 00:00:06,922
Michael needs to close legitimate deals before every operational detail

3
00:00:06,946 --> 00:00:07,734
is final.

4
00:00:08,054 --> 00:00:12,026
Define a separate readiness state and acceptance criteria together.

5
00:00:12,358 --> 00:00:15,698
The business problem comes before the choice of Salesforce tool.

6
00:00:16,746 --> 00:00:19,826
A Flow can respond to an approved state change, check

7
00:00:19,826 --> 00:00:23,218
prerequisites, and create a task for the correct owner.

8
00:00:23,524 --> 00:00:26,695
A validation rule can block an invalid save with a

9
00:00:26,695 --> 00:00:28,102
useful explanation.

10
00:00:28,409 --> 00:00:30,563
Each serves a different part of the design.

11
00:00:31,626 --> 00:00:34,381
Check whether the record entered the ready state rather than

12
00:00:34,381 --> 00:00:36,783
merely being edited while already ready.

13
00:00:37,085 --> 00:00:43,109
Plan duplicate prevention, ownership changes, reopening, failures, and permissions.

14
00:00:43,412 --> 00:00:47,140
Repeated events should not accidentally multiply the same work.

15
00:00:48,197 --> 00:00:50,816
Build and test in an appropriate sandbox.

16
00:00:51,136 --> 00:00:56,638
Test missing data, repeated updates, multiple users, bulk behavior, and

17
00:00:56,638 --> 00:00:57,942
connected workflows.

18
00:00:58,275 --> 00:01:04,228
Sandboxes can contain sensitive information or external connections, so isolation

19
00:01:04,228 --> 00:01:05,636
still needs to be checked.

20
00:01:06,716 --> 00:01:10,078
Michael and Olivia perform user acceptance testing.

21
00:01:10,414 --> 00:01:16,312
Investigate dependencies, document changes, obtain required approval, and plan recovery

22
00:01:16,312 --> 00:01:17,408
before release.

23
00:01:17,758 --> 00:01:22,224
After deployment, check important behavior again and teach users the

24
00:01:22,224 --> 00:01:23,268
new process.

25
00:01:24,319 --> 00:01:28,378
The source’s fictional handoff completeness rises from sixty two to

26
00:01:28,378 --> 00:01:29,747
ninety three percent.

27
00:01:30,079 --> 00:01:32,992
That is a thirty one percentage point difference, not an

28
00:01:32,992 --> 00:01:34,103
Axios result.

29
00:01:34,435 --> 00:01:39,474
Comparable periods, stable definitions, and other possible influences matter when

30
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:40,739
judging the improvement.
